<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia raises bread, semolina and pasta prices.</title>
<headline>Tunisia raises bread, semolina and pasta prices.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The prices of bread, semolina and pasta inched up in Tunisia on Monday after a government decision to raise the cost of some subsidised foodstuffs.</p>
<p>The price of a small loaf of bread (250 grammes), rose 10 millimes to 140 millimes (0.14 dinar), the Commerce Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>Semolina and flour were up 20 millimes per kg to 255 millimes and 325 millimes.</p>
<p>The price of pasta and couscous increased by 40 millimes per kg to 385 millimes and 425 millimes, the ministry said. ($=0.96 dinar)</p>
</text>
